The skills in this repository are original works. Several of them reimplement, in
original wording and structure, well-known engineering practices and workflow ideas
that have been popularized by the open-source Claude Code / agent-skills community —
notably staged spec→ticket flows, TDD-at-seams, dual-axis code review, throwaway
feasibility spikes, and red-repro-first bug diagnosis.

No third-party skill files are redistributed here. Where a practice was learned from
another author's open-source skill, credit is due to that community; the text in this
repository was written independently for this pack.

The TDD block was informed by Matt Pocock's MIT-licensed `tdd` skill:
https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/ed37663cc5fbef691ddfecd080dff42f7e7e350d/skills/engineering/tdd

The standalone implement orchestration boundary was informed by Matt Pocock's
MIT-licensed `implement` and `code-review` skills. harness-ship independently adds
pre-defined role routing, root-owned integration, fixed-point review, delivery
evidence, and recovery:
https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/ed37663cc5fbef691ddfecd080dff42f7e7e350d/skills/engineering/implement
https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/ed37663cc5fbef691ddfecd080dff42f7e7e350d/skills/engineering/code-review
